FG-054 / D2 (owner decision 2026-10-18): the PPTX export writes each embedded font's
real OS/2 fsType into its EOT header instead of 0 (Installable).

vcl/source/font/EOTConverter.cxx wrote nFsType = 0 for every font it embeds into
ppt/fonts/*.fntdata (upstream FIXME: "some TrueType fonts set it to an
over-restrictive value"). A re-embedded Editable (8) or Preview & Print (4) face
therefore came out labelled Installable: wider rights than the font grants. WASM
only; EOTConverter is compiled whether or not --enable-eot is set (it is the
encoder; libeot is the decoder).

--- a/vcl/source/font/EOTConverter.cxx
+++ b/vcl/source/font/EOTConverter.cxx
@@ -90,9 +90,17 @@
 
         pEot->nItalic = pOS2->nFsSelection & 0x01;
         pEot->nWeight = pOS2->nWeightClass;
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+        // FG-054 / D2: write the font's real OS/2 fsType into the EOT header. Writing 0
+        // (Installable) told every reader the font may be installed and edited freely,
+        // whatever its licence said: a re-embedded Preview & Print or Editable face came
+        // out as Installable. The rights are the font's, not ours to widen.
+        pEot->nFsType = pOS2->nFsType;
+#else
         // FIXME: Should use OS2->fsType, but some TrueType fonts set it to an over-restrictive value.
         // Since ATS does not enforce this on Mac OS X, we do not enforce it either.
         pEot->nFsType = 0x0000;
+#endif
         pEot->nUnicodeRange1 = pOS2->nUnicodeRange1;
         pEot->nUnicodeRange2 = pOS2->nUnicodeRange2;
         pEot->nUnicodeRange3 = pOS2->nUnicodeRange3;
